comment:
Observed the following areas in need of more frequent cleaning to prevent an accumulation of soil residues:
(i) the ventilation hood;
(ii) the walls behind the stove and small fryers;
(iii) the grate of the air conditioner near the ventilation hood;
(iv) the wall behind the mop sink; 
(v) the underside of the soda machine near the soda water nozzle;
(vi) the seam of the handwashing sink.
PIC was notified of these areas and plans to clean these areas at the next deep clean of the facility. Ensure that nonfood-contact surfaces of equipment and surfaces are cleaned at a frequency necessary to prevent an accumulation of soil residues.

Observed a deep container of sliced tomatoes (which are a Time/Temperature Control for Safety Food) which was measured at 47°F (probed), above 41°F. Tomatoes were prepared beyond the 4 hour cooling window to use time as a control. Other items in the fridge were sufficiently cold holding. CORRECTED: PIC voluntarily discarded the tomatoes. Inspector discussed with PIC and staff solutions for cooling prepared TCS produce:
(i) preparing smaller amounts of food that will cool faster; 
(ii) preparing shallower containers or smaller containers so that food can more easily disperse heat and cool faster; 
(iii) cooling the tomatoes in the walk-in cooler, which cools food more effectively, especially as the standing cooler in the kitchen area is frequently opened during service, making cooling difficult. 
(iv) store whole tomatoes under refrigeration to pre-cool them prior to cutting.
Ensure that all TCS Foods are cooled within 4 hours to 41°F or less when prepared from ingredients at ambient temperature.

Inspectors observed the following non-food-contact surfaces that need to be cleaned at more frequency:
(a) the bottom of the dry storage small cube reach-in freezer had an accumulation of chicken and pretzels;
(b) the undersides of the soda fountain; 
(c) the underside of the coffee maker basket.
PIC was informed and a plan was made to clean these areas more frequently to prevent the accumulation of soil residues.

